run/client-merged-pack/

# Gate bookkeeping: the pid of the server a gate started, so an interrupted run can be reaped by the next
# one. Per-rundir and worthless the moment the machine reboots — never commit it.
.forbric-gate.pid

# Gate rundirs created by gate-m10 / gate-m11. Nothing in a rundir needs to be committed: the launcher
# writes eula.txt when it is missing, the gates write their own server.properties and stage their own mods,
# and the server regenerates a fresh management-server-secret on every boot — which is why the rundirs that
# ARE tracked show up as noise in every diff.
run/server-config/
run/server-overlay/
